{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_017faa0cbaaf43ee23a1d3ec997a9dfb42a1d566b7437d275029ac48a5b64949"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every session gets construct's MCP tools, letting any harness spawn subagents, send them input, and read their output for agent-to-agent orchestration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_02011da69bbf74c81888bbae3faca43846633aa9a8c78a4f06a1e71fb4cdc6c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Construct wraps CLIs already on the machine; users must install and authenticate harnesses such as codex, claude, opencode, agy, grok, muse, and prime-agent, while smith is built in."},{"claim_ids":["clm_127af993f42400a88dd4141a77e2e2c5e02f31dad4eed105f7fe14e6e3dcd847"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Lineage lets sessions branch like ideas: a session can be forked for a parallel attempt, including cross-harness forks, and results merged back."},{"claim_ids":["clm_161bcf4eddb511af5b2f7ff00ae51ed2c69e4692e7f4292ab68abd5b64b771ab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions live in the daemon rather than the terminal, so SSH drops or laptop sleep do not stop agents, and users can reattach with scrollback intact."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1eca237c3520f8342d800282c4ad374bc38ecc2dcb9c110ec69fa8c2f95fcd42"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`/remote-control` opens a browser-accessible web client with a QR code so users can connect from a phone without service signup or setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ffc63cbc0879acdda1390af2392c9e6e1b71bf70bc50be7b539ca1d18fd655e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The daemon owns sessions, persists state, and exposes the local IPC socket used by clients; lifecycle helpers include daemon start/stop/restart with session-safe stop variants."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4d9c60a321fbb971b5ef835cfab111699ffb331093beebdc2ad24b6dccb01067"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The harness adapter protocol uses separate adapter processes speaking JSON-RPC over stdio, so new tools can plug in without changing the daemon."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58973e8fe85ab373e8755372f95391b1ac06356fb2abea79894a7de474fb6a4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Construct is a single Rust binary that includes a TUI, control CLI, daemon, ACP stdio server, an internal MCP bridge, and harness adapters."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8120fae9c74cc2c013fd43d002e3f8705a2e2fa1653f571606615604cd03424"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`construct acp` runs an Agent Client Protocol stdio server that auto-starts the daemon if needed and maps ACP session lifecycle calls onto daemon sessions, with --harness/--model/--cwd defaults."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f781504c28d792a98b1db39c555896954a53e7c1415b1f8ae0f0e1642040448f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The TUI supports `?` for help and `M-x` for a command palette, and users can create sessions, switch agents, send input, inspect diffs, and interrupt work from it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc9074d29ede2832838747342a54e50e667e6b6505a9de115bab1a05c57661bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running `construct` auto-starts a background daemon and attaches if none is running; this can be disabled with CONSTRUCT_NO_AUTOSTART=1."}],"claim_ids":["clm_017faa0cbaaf43ee23a1d3ec997a9dfb42a1d566b7437d275029ac48a5b64949","clm_02011da69bbf74c81888bbae3faca43846633aa9a8c78a4f06a1e71fb4cdc6c2","clm_127af993f42400a88dd4141a77e2e2c5e02f31dad4eed105f7fe14e6e3dcd847","clm_161bcf4eddb511af5b2f7ff00ae51ed2c69e4692e7f4292ab68abd5b64b771ab","clm_1eca237c3520f8342d800282c4ad374bc38ecc2dcb9c110ec69fa8c2f95fcd42","clm_3ffc63cbc0879acdda1390af2392c9e6e1b71bf70bc50be7b539ca1d18fd655e","clm_4d9c60a321fbb971b5ef835cfab111699ffb331093beebdc2ad24b6dccb01067","clm_58973e8fe85ab373e8755372f95391b1ac06356fb2abea79894a7de474fb6a4a","clm_c8120fae9c74cc2c013fd43d002e3f8705a2e2fa1653f571606615604cd03424","clm_f781504c28d792a98b1db39c555896954a53e7c1415b1f8ae0f0e1642040448f","clm_fc9074d29ede2832838747342a54e50e667e6b6505a9de115bab1a05c57661bd"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","id":"pg_5f1105